;; Regulatory source register for JPN-MOD (防衛省, Japan Ministry of Defense)
;; defense-equipment-transfer and security-clearance compliance.
;;
;; The README says the actor's facts.cljc is grounded in mod.go.jp / mofa.go.jp
;; / cas.go.jp / meti.go.jp / japaneselawtranslation.go.jp sources. Until this
;; file existed there was no citable list of WHICH sources those are, so no
;; claim in this repository could be traced to a fetched authority. This is
;; that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law or page not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or a
;; URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljk`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it:
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id   Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require
;;                   the title and the law number to still match. HTTP status
;;                   is never consulted here and must not be: laws.e-gov.go.jp
;;                   is a single-page app that answers HTTP 200 for
;;                   /law/<anything>, renders "not found" client-side, and
;;                   therefore cannot tell a real citation from an invented one.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; WHY NO PAGE ON www.mod.go.jp IS CITED HERE. Measured 2026-08-31: both
;; https://www.mod.go.jp/ and a deep path answer HTTP 403 to an automated
;; client with a 5639-byte "Just a moment..." Cloudflare challenge body at the
;; requested URL -- a bot challenge, not a refusal-by-status, and not a page.
;; The rule this register follows is that a host that refused to answer has
;; NOT been cited and has NOT been measured as absent: not-cited and absent
;; are different, and only the second could be recorded from a run that never
;; got past the edge. The register therefore records the mod.go.jp gap as a
;; :coverage entry below, and cites pages only on hosts this run actually
;; read: www.cas.go.jp and www.japaneselawtranslation.go.jp. The same applies
;; to www.mofa.go.jp (HTTP 403, 426-byte "Access Denied", Akamai edge).
;;
;; HOST ASSUMPTIONS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT.
;; The :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path
;; that does not exist. The verifier fetches a nonexistent path on every host
;; in the register and fails if the answer has changed. A dated note saying
;; "measured to refuse correctly" degrades into a constant the moment it is
;; written; a declaration the run re-measures cannot.
;;
;; WHY www.cas.go.jp IS IN A DEFENSE REGISTER. 内閣官房 (Cabinet Secretariat)
;; is the administrative authority behind BOTH of this repository's page-level
;; regimes that are not statutes: the designation of 特定秘密 under the
;; Specially-Designated-Secrets Act runs through designated organs centred on
;; the Cabinet Secretariat, and the security-clearance regime under the
;; Economic Security Act (重要経済安保情報の保護及び活用に関する法律) is
;; administered by 内閣官房's 经济安保推进本部. The MOD's own site is the
;; blocked host described above; the Cabinet Secretariat is the authority the
;; statutes point at that this run could actually read.
;;
;; 防衛装備移転三原則 IS NOT CITED, AND THAT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT. The Three
;; Principles on Transfer of Defense Equipment are a 閣議決定 (cabinet
;; decision, 2014-04-01, reaffirmed as 防衛装備移転三原則 in 2023-03-31
;;国家安全保障戦略 revision), not a statute: they have no e-Gov law id, and
;; the document lives on www.mod.go.jp -- the host that interposed a challenge
;; this run. A cabinet decision whose only official home is a host that
;; refuses automated clients cannot be cited on the strength of this run's
;; reads, so its absence is recorded in :coverage below.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in a defense-transfer / clearance
;; register. Claims stop at the level actually checked -- law identity, and
;; for the page entries the title, URL, charset, and the de-tagged strings
;; read on 2026-08-31. No article text is asserted, because none was read.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run. A change here invalidates the check that rests
 ;; on it, which is the point of writing it down as data.

 {:source/id "host.www-cas-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.cas.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "Re-measured 2026-08-31 with node fetch (the verifier's
                client): the front page answers 200 (14503 bytes, title
                `内閣官房ホームページ`) and the verifier's exact nonexistent
                path /no-such-page-zzz999.html answers 404 at the requested
                URL -- 6304 bytes, title `お探しのページが見つかりませんでし
                た。｜内閣官房ホームページ`, no redirect, no challenge. Note
                a directory-style missing path (no filename) answers 302
                instead; the verifier measures a filename-shaped path, and
                that is the behaviour declared here. http:// redirects to
                https, so the :unexpected-redirect self-test discriminates on
                this host. :refuses because the path is answered with a real
                status-and-body that is not the page asked for."}

 {:source/id "host.www-japaneselawtranslation-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.japaneselawtranslation.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "Re-measured 2026-08-31 with node fetch (the verifier's
                client): /laws/ answers 200 (44458 bytes UTF-8, title
                `Search by Title - Law Search - Japanese Law Translation`) and
                the verifier's exact nonexistent path answers 404 at the
                requested URL -- 1667 bytes, title `Error - Japanese Law
                Translation`, no redirect. http:// redirects to https, so the
                :unexpected-redirect self-test discriminates on this host too.
                :refuses because the path is answered with a real
                status-and-body that is not the page asked for."}

 ;; ── Coverage of what this register does NOT cite ─────────────────────────

 {:source/id "coverage.mod"
  :source/kind :coverage
  :coverage/entries 10
  :coverage/by-verify {:e-gov-law-id 5 :page-identity 4 :page-text 1}
  :source/note "5 statutes, 4 :page-identity entries, 1 :page-text entry, and
                2 :host-behaviour entities. NOT CITED, and why:
                (1) www.mod.go.jp pages (including 防衛装備移転三原則 and the
                調達 policy pages) -- the host interposed a 403 Cloudflare
                'Just a moment...' challenge to this run's automated client,
                so nothing on it was read and nothing is claimed;
                (2) www.mofa.go.jp pages -- HTTP 403 'Access Denied' (Akamai)
                for the same reason; (3) 防衛装備移転三原則 itself -- a 閣議決
                定, not a statute, with no e-Gov law id and its official text
                hosted only on the challenged mod.go.jp host. A later run with
                a browser-grade client that reads those hosts should MOVE these
                citations in; until then the gap is the finding, not an
                oversight."}

